WEBVTT

00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:11.200
"Kansai"

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:21.950
"Clock Out"

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:22.290
"No Entry"

00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:27.580
Nice! Out on time today!

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:29.290
"Kansai"
"Seal Center"

00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:31.540
"South Ward"
"Dotonbori"

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:36.000
Huh? A cat?

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:39.290
Hey, look out!

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:41.000
"Danger"

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:44.450
You got a death wish?!

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:47.290
S-Sorry!

00:00:47.290 --> 00:00:47.450
"Cutthroat Public Execution Today"

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:49.330
"South Ward"
"Back Alley"
"Cutthroat Public Execution Today"

00:00:49.330 --> 00:00:53.120
"Cutthroat Public Execution Today"

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:59.330
Hmm? <i>Takoyaki</i>?

00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:02.120
Haven't had that in forever...

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:04.540
Maybe I should!

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:05.040
--One, two, three, four...

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:08.160
--Excuse me! One <i>takoyaki</i>, please!
--One, two, three, four...

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:12.410
Here ya go! That'll be 500 yen, please!

00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:16.080
You too, dear!

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:18.790
--Here!
--Come again!

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:36.660
"Akudama Drive"

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:05.750
Um... What happened to the Akudama
and the people on the <i>Shinkansen</i>?

00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:09.120
They left for Kanto. That's all I know.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:11.500
I see...

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:13.160
And the uprising?

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:14.700
Check the Akudama list.

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:15.910
Huh?

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:20.250
"Akudama List"
"Count: 5625"
"In 13hr 16min: 1852 executed"

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:20.250
"Akudama List"
"Count: 5625"
"In 13hr 16min: 1852 executed"

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:20.250
There're so many!

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:21.950
There're so many!

00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:24.040
All killed yesterday.

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:25.000
Huh?

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:29.040
The rioters were declared Akudama and executed.

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:32.620
You're kidding! They were just regular people!

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:35.580
People we have a duty to protect!

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:39.160
Those "regular people" started an uprising.

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:42.330
They caused damage, and that's a fact.

00:03:42.330 --> 00:03:45.910
As a result, they were declared Akudama.

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:47.120
But--!

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:51.580
Executing the rioters
brought back peace to the city.

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:57.620
Kansai would have collapsed if nothing
was done, but Boss took action.

00:03:57.620 --> 00:03:59.950
But to kill them?!

00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:03.870
Senpai...

00:04:03.870 --> 00:04:08.080
What makes someone an Akudama?

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:11.250
"Kansai Special Communication Room"
"Sky Hall"

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:11.250
Good job suppressing the uprising.

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:12.950
Thank you.

00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:18.910
This will be reported to Kanto,
along with how well you handled it.

00:04:18.910 --> 00:04:20.750
I'm honored.

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:31.910
Feels like forever since I laid in bed!

00:04:31.910 --> 00:04:33.450
Huh?

00:04:33.450 --> 00:04:38.910
"Boss" "Calling"
"Decline" "Accept"

00:04:33.450 --> 00:04:38.910
Dude, leave me alone!
Go and spend time with your wife and kids!

00:04:41.370 --> 00:04:45.870
I wanna forget about work
and go home on time every day!

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:48.580
That's the best way to live!

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:52.540
Now then! Time to get started
making dinner for toni--

00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:56.870
Gah, that hurt!

00:04:58.000 --> 00:04:59.910
Hmm?

00:04:59.910 --> 00:05:01.870
What's this?

00:05:03.830 --> 00:05:07.290
Did someone mistake my bag for theirs?

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:13.160
Huh?! What the heck?! Get back--!

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:15.750
What?!

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:17.250
"Takoyaki"

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:17.250
What?!

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:19.370
"Takoyaki"

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:19.370
Huh? What's going on?

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:23.370
Five hundred yen?

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:27.160
It checks out.

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:32.200
He's just a kid, but I guess the legendary
Courier gets the job done.

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:33.910
Courier never fails.

00:05:33.910 --> 00:05:36.040
We sent the money.

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:39.700
Courier has confirmed the payment.

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:40.950
Good work.

00:05:40.950 --> 00:05:43.540
Here's your tip.

00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:46.000
Go buy candy or something.

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:10.830
Here ya go.

00:06:10.830 --> 00:06:12.750
Five hundred yen?

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:25.750
Hello! Bunny here!

00:06:25.750 --> 00:06:26.580
Huh?

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:29.620
'Sup?! It's Shark here!

00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:32.830
Hey, Shark! You know about
the "Butterfly Dream"?

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:34.330
Of course I do!

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:38.950
Did you dream you're a butterfly,
or are you a butterfly dreaming you?

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:41.000
You knew something for once!

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:46.080
Everyone knows it! So you don't
know which you are, right?

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:52.290
I'm... trying to give 500 yen back... Wait, huh?

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:56.410
See? You're not even sure!
Like you're inside a dream!

00:06:56.410 --> 00:07:00.790
You can't tell what's real and
what's a dream anymore, right?

00:07:00.790 --> 00:07:03.910
But from now on, everything is real!

00:07:03.910 --> 00:07:09.950
This nowhere place! This timeless now!
This is where you truly belong!

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:14.160
Lots of bad things happened
and a lot of things you regret!

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:20.250
But here, none of it is true!
The only thing that's real is happiness!

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:22.200
Only happiness?

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:25.160
Yup! Only happiness!

00:07:25.160 --> 00:07:29.950
You can be the happiest
you've ever been--forever!

00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:35.830
You can soak in happy feelings all day long!

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:39.200
Bed feels amazing!

00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:42.160
Relive the good times, over and over!

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:44.450
Time to make <i>okonomiyaki</i>!

00:07:44.450 --> 00:07:48.500
Enjoy your fondest memories
whenever you want! That's--

00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:49.870
Whoa!

00:07:51.290 --> 00:07:52.660
Hmm?

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:57.410
Here ya go. Come again.

00:07:58.870 --> 00:08:01.950
Um, did you drop this coin?

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:05.500
Why, thank you!

00:08:05.500 --> 00:08:06.580
Huh?

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:14.290
Courier!

00:08:14.290 --> 00:08:18.410
I've been trying to give you
this money back for so long!

00:08:18.410 --> 00:08:21.950
I'm so glad you finally took it!

00:08:23.620 --> 00:08:26.250
Lemme tell you something.

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:32.330
Lemme tell you something.

00:08:32.330 --> 00:08:34.500
She...

00:08:34.500 --> 00:08:36.410
Courier...

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:39.750
...has a rotten mouth!

00:08:47.410 --> 00:08:49.410
Huh?

00:08:49.410 --> 00:08:51.540
What... the... heck?!

00:08:56.830 --> 00:08:59.160
Huh?! What's happening?!

00:09:07.700 --> 00:09:10.750
It's... the <i>Shinkansen</i>?!

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:12.620
Courier!

00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:18.120
--Whoa!
--I finally linked up to your channel.

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:19.950
--I finally linked up to your channel.

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:23.950
It's a good thing you guys
had that coin in common.

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:27.250
That voice! Is that you, Hacker?!

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:32.910
It's not very nice to point your gun at me.
Not when I saved your asses.

00:09:32.910 --> 00:09:35.200
I'm glad to hear you're okay!

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:38.620
Where are you? Are you
watching us from somewhere?

00:09:38.620 --> 00:09:41.080
You're half right and half wrong.

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:47.660
You're right that I've been watching you,
and wrong because I'm nowhere.

00:09:47.660 --> 00:09:49.080
What's that mean?

00:09:49.080 --> 00:09:50.330
How it sounds.

00:09:50.330 --> 00:09:53.250
Anyways, can you explain what's going on?

00:09:53.250 --> 00:09:56.870
Wasn't I in Kansai?
And I just saw Bunny and Shark!

00:09:56.870 --> 00:10:02.370
The ones from that educational program thing!
And where's everyone else?!

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:05.700
That program was made for brainwashing.

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:10.370
It's a way to separate the body
and mind of those coming to Kanto.

00:10:10.370 --> 00:10:13.290
It's the truth behind the Decontamination Zone.

00:10:13.290 --> 00:10:18.330
Huh? The program is the Decontamination Zone?
What do you mean by "truth"?

00:10:18.330 --> 00:10:21.290
You two were inside it just now.

00:10:21.290 --> 00:10:26.120
If I hadn't helped, you would've been
trapped in Kanto with the others.

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:31.000
Huh? Trapped in Kanto?

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:35.250
Sister? Where's Sister?! And Brother!

00:10:39.620 --> 00:10:41.540
The vault!

00:10:41.540 --> 00:10:46.870
What'd you expect?
Those kids are what Kanto wanted.

00:10:46.870 --> 00:10:50.660
More importantly, why don't you look outside?

00:10:58.910 --> 00:11:00.540
Whoa...

00:11:00.540 --> 00:11:01.870
This is Kanto?

00:11:01.870 --> 00:11:02.950
<i>This </i>is?!

00:11:02.950 --> 00:11:06.080
You're not wrong, but you're not right.

00:11:06.080 --> 00:11:09.200
I'll show you the true form of Kanto.

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:12.120
Huh?! Does it work like that?!

00:11:12.120 --> 00:11:15.450
Did he just do that like it's nothing?

00:11:27.250 --> 00:11:29.080
What's that?

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:34.870
What is it?

00:11:34.870 --> 00:11:39.120
This here... is Kanto.

00:11:39.120 --> 00:11:42.620
This here? Kanto?

00:11:42.620 --> 00:11:47.200
Hold up! What about this
weird place? I'm totally lost!

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:53.410
After the war, the people of Kanto
began converting their minds into data.

00:11:53.410 --> 00:11:57.330
Storing and preserving that
much data proved challenging,

00:11:57.330 --> 00:12:00.160
so they created this vessel to hold it.

00:12:00.160 --> 00:12:04.250
This... is a quantum supercomputer.

00:12:04.250 --> 00:12:06.000
Quantum?

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:10.040
You mean, the people of Kanto are inside this?

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:13.160
It's a utopia compared to Kansai, right?

00:12:13.160 --> 00:12:15.580
Were you trapped by Kanto, too?

00:12:15.580 --> 00:12:21.950
Being a genius, I protected my mind data
before getting taken by Kanto.

00:12:23.910 --> 00:12:28.000
As you can see, I haven't forgot my appearance.

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:31.620
Anyways, what a crazy twist, right?

00:12:31.620 --> 00:12:34.950
A world inside a quantum supercomputer.

00:12:34.950 --> 00:12:39.540
Who would've thought Kanto
would be some overused sci-fi trope?

00:12:39.540 --> 00:12:43.830
Kanto wasn't all that you'd hoped it would be.

00:12:45.410 --> 00:12:50.540
Enough about this crazy Kanto stuff!
We've gotta find the children!

00:12:50.540 --> 00:12:55.040
What are you talking about?
They've been up there the whole time.

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:56.370
Huh?

00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:13.370
Sister! Brother!

00:13:13.370 --> 00:13:14.830
What's happening?

00:13:14.830 --> 00:13:21.660
What's it doing to them? What are they
to Kanto?! Answer me, Hacker!

00:13:21.660 --> 00:13:28.410
No matter how amazing their technology,
there's something even Kanto can't escape.

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:33.870
And that's deterioration
over the span of many years.

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:37.660
So they researched and built an ideal housing.

00:13:37.660 --> 00:13:40.250
You don't mean...

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:45.160
Kanto is gonna get put... inside them?!

00:13:45.160 --> 00:13:51.080
Correct. As we speak, all of Kanto's data
is being transferred to their minds.

00:13:51.080 --> 00:13:57.450
When that circle turns white...
Kanto's transfer will be complete.

00:13:57.450 --> 00:14:03.500
With this, Kanto will be the perfect
utopia they always yearned for.

00:14:14.870 --> 00:14:16.500
It's impossible.

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:22.700
There's a gravitational wave defense program
around the cube and children.

00:14:22.700 --> 00:14:25.370
It's impossible to save 'em from here.

00:14:25.370 --> 00:14:27.830
You've gotta be kidding me!

00:14:27.830 --> 00:14:32.540
So the only reason they were born
was to be used by Kanto?!

00:14:32.540 --> 00:14:37.660
They're parts needed for Kanto to last forever.

00:14:37.660 --> 00:14:43.870
Those kids have fought against
all odds running away from Kanto.

00:14:43.870 --> 00:14:47.750
Struggling to find a place where they belong.

00:14:47.750 --> 00:14:52.000
This is where they belong more than anywhere.
Maybe you're overthinking--

00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:54.410
This?!

00:14:54.410 --> 00:14:59.040
This...? This is where they belong?!

00:15:00.660 --> 00:15:03.200
Being used like objects...

00:15:03.200 --> 00:15:05.870
Suffering so much...

00:15:05.870 --> 00:15:09.750
Terrified of the place "they belong"?

00:15:09.750 --> 00:15:14.870
Those kids... All they want is to be together.

00:15:14.870 --> 00:15:18.580
It's the only thing they want in their lives!

00:15:18.580 --> 00:15:24.500
Is it wrong of them to wanna make
that little dream come true?!

00:15:24.500 --> 00:15:29.500
Why can't they decide where
they belong on their own?!

00:15:29.500 --> 00:15:34.000
If that's the case, I'm not gonna stand for it!

00:15:37.080 --> 00:15:41.870
You talk big for someone
who happily dove into bed.

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:51.040
Didn't Kanto let you be with
someone you can't forget?

00:15:51.040 --> 00:15:53.450
That's revolting.

00:15:53.450 --> 00:15:56.410
My memories are mine alone.

00:15:59.870 --> 00:16:03.660
Wait for me... I'm coming...

00:16:04.540 --> 00:16:09.830
I'm going to save you guys, even if it kills me!

00:16:11.040 --> 00:16:13.750
You're gonna be so damn free...

00:16:13.750 --> 00:16:19.040
...that you can tell this shitty world
"Serves you right!" and laugh in its face!

00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:22.200
I've already made up my mind!

00:16:22.200 --> 00:16:26.330
And nobody--nobody--is gonna stop me!

00:16:34.620 --> 00:16:39.870
I said it's impossible to save the kids
from here. You got ears?

00:16:39.870 --> 00:16:41.750
Hacker?

00:16:44.370 --> 00:16:46.660
Interesting, isn't it?

00:16:46.660 --> 00:16:49.950
Monitoring you guys, I realized something.

00:16:49.950 --> 00:16:50.660
Huh?

00:16:50.660 --> 00:16:55.370
You're all stupid, selfish, and egotistical.

00:16:55.370 --> 00:16:57.540
Hacker? What are you...?

00:16:57.540 --> 00:17:01.410
This is thanks for returning
my drone as promised.

00:17:01.410 --> 00:17:02.620
Huh?

00:17:02.620 --> 00:17:05.580
It'll be perfect to stave the boredom.

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:11.410
Hacker?! Where did you go?!

00:17:11.410 --> 00:17:15.000
Didn't you hear? You can't
save the kids from there.

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:15.870
And?

00:17:15.870 --> 00:17:19.620
But for me inside Kanto, I've got a chance.

00:17:19.620 --> 00:17:21.870
Damn close to zero though.

00:17:21.870 --> 00:17:25.080
Why do it? What's in it for you?

00:17:26.040 --> 00:17:28.120
I'm just thanking Swindler.

00:17:28.120 --> 00:17:32.200
Besides, this might finally
be a game that satisfies me.

00:17:32.200 --> 00:17:34.540
Hacker.

00:17:34.540 --> 00:17:36.870
I believe in you!

00:17:36.870 --> 00:17:39.370
Sure you're not swindling me?

00:17:49.700 --> 00:17:53.330
Let's do this! It's game time!

00:17:58.700 --> 00:18:01.620
This goes deeper than I thought!

00:18:07.910 --> 00:18:10.160
Talk about a firewall!

00:18:13.040 --> 00:18:14.410
Found 'em!

00:18:19.790 --> 00:18:21.700
Surf's up!

00:18:34.330 --> 00:18:37.290
To think--me, getting my ass kicked!

00:18:37.290 --> 00:18:40.290
Now <i>this </i>is freakin' exciting!

00:18:58.120 --> 00:19:01.950
Game... over, huh?

00:19:11.330 --> 00:19:12.950
That's...

00:19:22.950 --> 00:19:26.160
Those Kanto idiots.

00:19:26.160 --> 00:19:29.410
You shouldn't have made the kids self-aware!

00:20:08.450 --> 00:20:12.040
Did you enjoy your game?

00:20:20.290 --> 00:20:23.950
Wake up! Wake up! Open your eyes!

00:20:29.540 --> 00:20:32.410
Big Sis...

00:20:46.000 --> 00:20:50.040
You idiot! Why didn't you run away?!

00:20:50.040 --> 00:20:53.870
Because nothing matters if I'm not with you.

00:20:58.830 --> 00:21:00.910
Brother, here!

00:21:03.080 --> 00:21:06.120
You really looked after it for me!

00:21:06.120 --> 00:21:07.700
Guess it went well.

00:21:07.700 --> 00:21:10.950
Yup! You okay, Hacker?

00:21:10.950 --> 00:21:13.120
Yeah.

00:21:13.120 --> 00:21:15.040
Just fine.

00:21:16.120 --> 00:21:20.950
Hurry up and get on the <i>Shinkansen</i>.
I'll send it back to Kansai.

00:21:20.950 --> 00:21:22.790
What about you?

00:21:24.500 --> 00:21:26.160
"Sender: Hacker"
"Subject: Gift for the Afterlife"

00:21:24.500 --> 00:21:26.160
What's this?

00:21:26.160 --> 00:21:28.200
"Sender: Hacker"
"Subject: Gift for the Afterlife"

00:21:26.160 --> 00:21:28.200
A gift for the afterlife.

00:21:28.200 --> 00:21:31.080
I found it in some pre-war literature.

00:21:31.080 --> 00:21:36.370
It's a mystical place nobody's
heard about, let alone been to.

00:21:36.370 --> 00:21:39.540
A perfect place for you guys.

00:21:39.540 --> 00:21:44.700
Hacker, you give gifts for the
afterlife to people passing away.

00:21:44.700 --> 00:21:46.750
But thank you.

00:21:55.040 --> 00:21:57.160
What are you doing? Let's go.

00:21:57.160 --> 00:21:58.540
Right.

00:21:59.330 --> 00:22:01.580
"Shinkansen"
"Carriage 1: Vault Car"

00:22:02.830 --> 00:22:06.330
Without solid ground,
bikes are just a pretty toy.

00:22:06.330 --> 00:22:08.200
We can hear your heart talking.

00:22:08.200 --> 00:22:09.790
Brother.

00:22:14.950 --> 00:22:17.620
I guess your job is over now?

00:22:17.620 --> 00:22:18.580
Yeah.

00:22:18.580 --> 00:22:23.290
Thanks for everything.
It was worth every last penny of mine.

00:22:23.290 --> 00:22:24.790
It's chump change.

00:22:24.790 --> 00:22:28.410
Not even the richest person would say that!

00:22:28.410 --> 00:22:30.000
What's your plan now?

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:32.500
This time, I'll protect you!

00:22:32.500 --> 00:22:33.200
--No! I promised to protect you first!

00:22:33.200 --> 00:22:35.660
--I think I'll take a gamble and head to this place.
--No! I promised to protect you first!

00:22:35.660 --> 00:22:36.450
